# 📦 8. Package Management

Linux Mint uses APT for package management.

### Update package information

```bash
sudo apt update
```

### Upgrade installed packages

```bash
sudo apt upgrade
```

### Install a package

```bash
sudo apt install package-name
```

### Remove a package

```bash
sudo apt remove package-name
```

### Search for a package

```bash
apt search package-name
```

### Show installed packages

```bash
apt list --installed
```

---

# ⚙️ 9. Process Management

### `ps`

Displays running processes.

```bash
ps aux
```

### `top`

Provides a live view of running processes.

```bash
top
```

### `kill`

Stops a process using its process ID.

```bash
kill PID
```

### `pkill`

Stops processes by name.

```bash
pkill process-name
```

